# The Ancient One: "{2}{U}{B}: Draw a card, then discard a card. When you discard a card this way, target player mills cards equal to
# its mana value." Turn 3: Bot1 discards a Hill Giant (mana value four) and targets itself: four cards go from its own library to its
# graveyard, five with the Hill Giant. Turn 5: Bot1 discards a Plains (mana value zero) and targets Bot2: the reflexive ability
# (CR 603.12) still goes on the stack, and Bot2 mills no card (CR 202.3, 701.17a). Bot2 plays a land each turn so never has to discard.

